{"message":"Success","data":{"uuid":"N2732698","newswiz_id":"2732698","published_at":1795208245,"tags":[],"main_tag":null,"category":{"id":4,"name":"Sports","is_main":1,"is_followed":false,"is_notify":false},"country":{"id":1,"name":"Saudi Arabia"},"city":{"id":3,"name":"Mecca","country_id":1},"default_image_url":null,"locale":"en","title":"Al-Ahli Defeats Al-Nassr 3-1 in Saudi Pro League Round 9","subtitle":null,"content":"Jeddah, November 20, 2026, SPA -- Al-Ahli defeated visiting Al-Nassr 3-1 today at King Abdullah Sports City Stadium in Jeddah in a postponed Round 9 Saudi Pro League (Roshn Saudi League) match.\n    Al-Nassr opened the scoring with Portuguese player Cristiano Ronaldo scoring in the 14th minute before Al-Ahli's Galeno equalized in the 45+1 minute, ending the first half in a 1-1 draw.\n    In the second half, Al-Ahli maintained its attacking pressure and took the lead through Ivan Toney, who converted a penalty kick in the 71st minute. Roger Ibañez extended the lead with a third goal in the 75th minute, securing a 3-1 victory for Al-Ahli.\n    With this result, Al-Ahli raised its tally to 24 points, provisionally occupying fourth place, while Al-Nassr remained on 28 points in third place.\n    -- SPA\r\n23:57 Local Time 20:57 GMT\r\n0089","hashtags":[{"id":548,"name":"Jeddah","locale":"en","created_at":"2023-12-17T10:13:36.000000Z","updated_at":"2023-12-17T10:13:36.000000Z"},{"id":8254,"name":"Saudi Pro League","locale":"en","created_at":"2024-08-25T16:56:59.000000Z","updated_at":"2024-08-25T16:56:59.000000Z"},{"id":18889,"name":"Al-Ahli","locale":"en","created_at":"2025-04-29T18:26:37.000000Z","updated_at":"2025-04-29T18:26:37.000000Z"}],"royal_news_types":[],"date_hijri":"1448-06-10","is_report":false,"related_news":[],"parent_news":null,"report_tasks":[],"translations":[{"uuid":"N2732651","locale":"ar"}],"media_images":{"attachment_display":1,"files":[{"id":4606340,"file":{"id":4677518,"uuid":"M11281511","path":"https://portalcdn.spa.gov.sa/back